1
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:18,860
Sports such as football, tennis and golf are popular all over the world with millions of people playing them or watching them on TV.

2
00:00:20,070 --> 00:00:24,600
But there are also many unusual sports that are not so well known.

3
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:27,560
Here are four interesting examples.

4
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:41,700
Every year, on a small Chinese island, thousands of people arrive to celebrate a very special event: the Cheung Chau bun festival.

5
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:48,120
The highlight of the festival is a race to the top of a very strange mountain.

6
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:54,760
The mountain is made of metal and covered with a type of traditional Chinese bun.

7
00:00:56,216 --> 00:01:03,120
Spectators watch as three teams compete to see how many buns they can take from the mountain.

8
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:11,007
The climb can be quite dangerous and people who want to take part must take a special training course.

9
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:21,340
Camel racing is a popular sport in many countries around the world, including Mongolia and Australia.

10
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:35,190
But it is especially popular in the Middle East and each year, from late October to early April, many big races take place in countries such as the United Arab Emirates.

11
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:42,380
As many as 70 camels race along sandy desert tracks for up to 16 km.

12
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:52,020
The owners of the camels drive by the side of the animals shouting at them to run faster and cross the finish line before the others.

13
00:01:55,660 --> 00:02:00,720
Bossaball is a very modern sport that was first played in 2005.

14
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:07,640
It started in Spain, but it was the idea of a Belgian man called Filip Eyckmans.

15
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:17,980
He wanted to create a sport that mixed together football, gymnastics, volleyball and the Brazilian music of bossa nova.

16
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,431
There are two trampolines with a net between them.

17
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:29,629
The idea is for one team to hit the ball over the net and the other team to try and hit it back.

18
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:37,060
The trampolines let the players jump very high, making the sport very exciting to watch.

19
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:48,182
The sport is already popular in many countries around the world, including Brazil, Mexico, Turkey, Singapore and Saudi Arabia.

20
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:55,763
Chess boxing was the invention of Dutch artist Iepe Rubingh.

21
00:02:56,600 --> 00:03:06,665
His original idea was to create a piece of performance art, but it was so popular that it soon became a sport played in countries all over the world.

22
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:08,600
The game is quite simple.

23
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:13,520
Two contestants compete against each other at chess and boxing.

24
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:25,200
Each round of chess is followed by a round of boxing with a break of a minute between each round to give the players time to put on or take off their gloves.

25
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:31,140
The first person to win either the chess match or the boxing match wins the game.
